# Applies to BOTH image builds: each runs with the repository root as the
# context (`docker build -f Dockerfile .` / `-f web/Dockerfile .`), and
# BuildKit only reads `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile or
# this root file, never a `.dockerignore` in a subdirectory.
#
# Unlike .gitignore, a pattern without a leading `**/` matches only at the
# context root. Build outputs, dependencies, local dev data and secrets can
# sit in any package (`web/node_modules`, `web/.next`, `crates/*/target`,
# `crates/server/.dev-data`), so those match at any depth.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.dev-data/
**/secrets/
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
docs/
fixtures/
*.md
!README.md
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
